# Per-attempt working state that is RECONSTRUCTIBLE and therefore not versioned.
#
# Policy (recorded 2026-09-20 by the integration step): every attempt keeps its
# summary evidence (run-all.txt, failures.txt, per-case JSON summaries, hashes,
# changes.diff, docs) in git, but NOT:
#   * iso/            - venvs and byte-identical product copies (rebuilt from HEAD
#                       + changes.diff; a venv must never be versioned)
#   * cmd-*/runs-*/   - pytest/sim per-command scratch workspaces
#   * prefix_src/     - pre-image source copies
#   * quarantine*/    - superseded scratch retained on disk only
#   * *-E5*/          - per-tree CLI case workspaces
#   * evidence/run/   - per-case sim run directories (the summaries above are kept)
#   * harness/scratch/
# This keeps each attempt reviewable (hashes + summaries) without committing
# hundreds of megabytes of working copies. Anything needed to reproduce a number
# is named in the attempt's commands.json / review.md.
*/a*/iso/
*/a*/before/cmd-*/
*/a*/before/prefix_src/
*/a*/before/runs*/
*/a*/before/quarantine*/
*/a*/after/cmd-*/
*/a*/after/runs*/
*/a*/after/quarantine*/
*/a*/r2/*-E5*/
*/a*/r2/cmd-*/
*/a*/r2/quarantine*/
*/a*/r2/runs-*/
*/a*/evidence/run/
*/a*/harness/scratch/
# Import-staging trees used to load TWO registry variants side by side under
# distinct module names. Rebuilt deterministically by the attempt's
# scripts/compute_compat.py from (a) the production pre-image and (b) iso/,
# so they are reconstructible and must not be versioned.
*/a*/_scratch_import/
# Scratch GIT REPOSITORIES created inside attempts (e.g. `git init` + `git apply`
# diff-apply checks). They must never be versioned AND must never be traversed by
# the parent repository: an embedded `.git` makes git treat the directory as a
# submodule, which breaks `git status` / `git add` and made the pre-push hook's
# stash/checkout sequence fail (see the 20260920 production-rollback incident in
# `_isolation_incidents/`). Ignoring them keeps the scratch trees on disk while
# keeping parent git operations healthy.
*/a*/r5/diff-apply-check/
*/a*/r5/diff-repo/

# deep pytest basetemp trees (Windows MAX_PATH) - too long to index
*/a*/after/falsified-normal-r1/
*/a*/after/runs-*/

# Nested verification repos (apply/diff/recovery round-trips) created by card
# harnesses — same class as the r5 rules above (added 2026-09-22 after finding
# 4 accidental mode-160000 gitlinks under I-14-D/a20260919-01):
#   never versioned AND never traversed by the parent repo.
*/a*/scratch/diff-repo*/
*/a*/scratch/apply-check/
*/a*/recovery/recovery-tree-*/

# Byte-identical product reference copies at non-standard depth (same policy class
# as */a*/iso/ above — reconstructible from HEAD + changes.diff; found staged by
# batch-2 sanity check 2026-09-22): */a*/b3_reference/iso/
*/b3_reference/iso/
